  "notes": "Address: diag-poke's VCP 0xEA/0xEB. SET 0xEE = byte (<= 0xFF) written with sub_23D9E7 when the address is in 0x101C00-0x101DFF; GET 0xEE reads with sub_23D972 (0xFFFF outside the bank and for the data port 0x101C66). RAM 0x2024B0 counts accepted writes, 0x2024B1 = 1 after a refused one. Only OSD display state can change; a redraw or power cycle restores it. v2: an open menu is no longer closed by SETs of VCP 0xEA-0xEE (the vendor closes it on any SET, 0x26B211). v3/v4: SET 0xEE = 0x100 loads the built-in 2-bit test glyphs (v4: even codes 0x3D0-0x3DE, RAM word 0x880 + 12 x code) with the firmware loaders' register sequence; 0x200 | row places the test row in window 1 with the firmware's tile routine 0x25C8F5; RAM 0x2024B2 counts completed commands. Generated by tools/patches_src_diag_osd.py."
